# AC 11 - two jobs due in the same minute. One runs, then the other. Not
# interleaved.
#
# Run this with a model that does not think first:
#     drive.py row-11-two-at-once.steps qwen2.5:7b
#
# The first attempt used qwen3.5:9b and never reached the criterion. Turns ran
# two to five minutes, so the session was mid-turn at nearly every boundary and
# the second job never got a gap to run in - which demonstrated AC 10 a third
# time and AC 11 not at all. Both jobs have to come due, run and finish inside a
# minute for the ordering to be visible, and that needs seconds-long turns.
#
# What should happen: at the boundary `due()` returns both, `_next_line` takes
# the older, and the second cannot start until that whole turn has ended - so
# the transcript reads ALPHA, its reply, BRAVO, its reply. Never a scheduled
# line inside somebody else's answer.

wait: 8
send: Schedule a repeating prompt, every minute, whose text is exactly: say ALPHA
wait: 40

send: Schedule a second repeating prompt, every minute, whose text is exactly: say BRAVO
wait: 40
mark: === AC 11 below: both due every minute from here. Nothing is typed ===

idle: 200
mark: === AC 11 above ===
send: /exit
